Does anybody out there remember what used to happen when one ate a
quantum mechanic corpse in ol' hack? If my memory serves me well, one
got a message to the effect that one's position seemed very uncertain.
At the time I didn't know what it meant, but I now believe one
received intrinsic displacement. It's nice to be able to receive intrinsic
speed from a Q in nethack, but I don't understand why the possibility
of gaining intrinsic displacement was removed. Quantum mechanistically, it
would make sense to be able to receive either intrinsic. So if the
following idea generates enough interest among the nethaddict community,
I will formally submit it to the dev team. The idea is the following:

If you have neither intrinsic speed nor displacement, eating a Q would
give you one of the two (50/50 to decide which). (Perhaps eating Werner's 
corpse could give you both!)

If you have either intrinsic speed or displacement, but not both, eating
a Q would give you a 50% chance of gaining the other intrinsic, otherwise
you would lose the one you have. (Eating Werner's corpse could flip the
intrinsics: if you have displacement, you lose it and gain speed, and vice
versa.)

If you have both intrinsics, eating a Q would remove one of them (50/50 to
decide which). (Eating Werner's corpse would remove both.)

In all cases, wearing a cloak of displacement would still give you
displacement regardless of whether you have the displacement intrinsic.
Gaining/losing speed would work as it currently does, with the possibility
of being normal, fast or ultrafast. With this whole scheme, being greedy and
wanting both intrinsics could take time and require you to eat a lot of Q's,
as you could waste a lot of corpses gaining one intrinsic, and losing it
again trying to get the other one. It would make the whole thing more
uncertain, which is the whole point, isn't it?

Let me know what you think!

